---
// NOTE FOR THE CLIENT: these terms are a good faith template written to match how
// this website actually works today. They are not legal advice, I am not a
// lawyer, and they should be reviewed by a qualified lawyer before launch,
// especially the limitation of liability and governing law sections.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Terms and Conditions | The Indian Kitchen, Toronto";
const description =
  "The terms that apply when you use The Indian Kitchen website, covering menu and pricing information, third party ordering, catering inquiries and liability.";

const lastUpdated = "29 July 2026";
const EMAIL = "hello@theindiankitchen.ca";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  {/* PAGE HEAD: compact band, clears the fixed header, no full screen hero. */}
  <section class="bg-green text-beige pt-32 md:pt-48 pb-14 md:pb-20">
    <div class="container-x max-w-3xl text-center mx-auto">
      <span class="inline-block text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.45em] text-saffron">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl mt-6 leading-[1.05]">
        Terms and Conditions
      </h1>
      <div class="mt-7 flex items-center justify-center gap-3 text-saffron">
        <span class="h-px w-10 bg-saffron/50"></span>
        <span class="size-2 rotate-45 border border-saffron"></span>
        <span class="h-px w-10 bg-saffron/50"></span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-beige/60">
        Last updated, {lastUpdated}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* TERMS BODY */}
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 bg-cream-pattern text-olive">
    <div class="container-x">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto legal-prose">
        <p class="text-lg">
          These terms apply to your use of the website of The Indian Kitchen, Biryani
          and Dosa, a restaurant at 3334 Yonge St, North York, Toronto, ON M4N 2M4. By
          browsing this site you accept them. If you do not agree with them, please do
          not use the site.
        </p>

        <h2>What this website is</h2>
        <p>
          This site is here to show you who we are and what we cook. Everything on it,
          the menu, dish descriptions, prices, photographs, opening hours and event
          information, is provided for general information. We keep it as accurate as
          we reasonably can, but it may change at any time without notice, and it may
          occasionally be out of date or contain errors.
        </p>
        <p>
          Photographs are of our food, but presentation and portions vary from plate to
          plate. Treat images as an impression of a dish rather than a promise about
          how it will arrive.
        </p>

        <h2>Prices and availability</h2>
        <p>
          Prices shown on this site are indicative. They are not an offer, and they are
          not guaranteed. The price you pay and whether a dish is available are
          confirmed at the point of order, whether that is in the restaurant, over the
          phone or on a delivery platform. Where a price here differs from the price at
          the point of order, the point of order price applies.
        </p>
        <p>
          Menu items can sell out, come off the menu seasonally, or change in
          preparation. Dietary and allergen notes on this site are a guide only. Our
          kitchen handles nuts, dairy, gluten and other allergens, and we cannot
          guarantee that any dish is free of them. If you have an allergy or a dietary
          requirement, speak to us directly before you order.
        </p>

        <h2>Ordering and delivery</h2>
        <p>
          You cannot place an order or pay on this website. Our order links take you to
          third party platforms, currently Uber Eats and DoorDash. Once you are there,
          your order is a contract between you and that platform, subject to their
          terms, their pricing, their fees and their privacy policies. Delivery times,
          delivery fees, driver conduct, refunds and order accuracy on those platforms
          are handled under their rules, and we do not control them.
        </p>

        <h2>Catering inquiries and reservations</h2>
        <p>
          Submitting the catering form, the contact form or the reservation form sends
          us a request. It is not a booking, and it does not commit us to anything.
          Nothing is confirmed until someone from the restaurant replies to you and
          confirms it directly. Availability, final pricing, deposits and any other
          arrangements for an event are agreed in that conversation, not on this
          website.
        </p>
        <p>
          We may decline a request, and we may need to change or cancel an arrangement
          if circumstances require it. If that happens we will tell you as soon as we
          can.
        </p>

        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
          Please use this site lawfully and reasonably. Do not attempt to interfere
          with it, gain unauthorised access to it, scrape it at a scale that affects
          its operation, or submit content through our forms that is unlawful,
          abusive or deliberately false.
        </p>

        <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The Indian Kitchen name, logo, brand, and the content of this site including
          text, dish descriptions, photographs, design, layout and code, belong to The
          Indian Kitchen or are used with permission. You may view the site, and share
          links to it. You may not copy, reproduce, republish or use our content or
          branding for commercial purposes without our written permission.
        </p>

        <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>
          This site links out to third parties, including delivery platforms, Google
          Maps and Instagram. Those links are provided for convenience. We are not
          responsible for the content, terms or practices of any site we link to.
        </p>

        <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          This website is provided as it is. We do not warrant that it will always be
          available, uninterrupted or free of errors.
        </p>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, The Indian Kitchen is not liable for
          any loss or damage arising from your use of this website, from reliance on
          information published on it, or from your dealings with any third party
          platform we link to. This includes indirect and consequential loss, such as
          lost profit or lost opportunity.
        </p>
        <p>
          Nothing in these terms limits or excludes any liability that cannot lawfully
          be limited or excluded, including liability for death or personal injury
          caused by negligence, or for fraud. Nothing here affects your statutory
          rights as a consumer under Ontario or Canadian law.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms from time to time. The current version is always
          the one published here, with the date shown at the top of this page.
          Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the updated
          terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Ontario and the
          federal laws of Canada that apply in it. Any dispute relating to this website
          or to these terms falls to the courts of Ontario, Canada.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact us</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms can go to
          <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>, or by post to The Indian Kitchen,
          3334 Yonge St, North York, Toronto, ON M4N 2M4, Canada.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
